The restriction in (P7) prevents overclaiming: the result is a theorem about the compactified weak-coupling families where the semiclassical constructions and scale separations are controlled, not a derivation for arbitrary strongly coupled four-dimensional Yang-Mills.

\noindent\textbf{Final Result.}
\[
\boxed{o=(o_{\rm QM},o_{\rm 2d})\in\Sigma_{\rm QM}\times\Sigma_{\rm 2d}\quad\text{within the controlled compactified weak-coupling regimes.}}
\]
\hfill$\blacksquare$
